Sure, I would pick the following individuals:

1. Leonardo da Vinci - A universal genius who mastered many fields including painting, sculpture, architecture, science, music etc.;
2. Albert Einstein - A theoretical physicist whose theories have profoundly changed our understanding of physical reality;
3. Marie Curie - A physical chemist and a pioneer in radioactivity research, the first woman Nobel laureate;
4. Confucius - An ancient Chinese philosopher whose ideas were revolutionary during his time;
5. Thomas Edison - An inventor and businessman who made many crucial contributions to mass communication and technology.

These figures represent different time periods and areas of human endeavor, reflecting the broad scope of human intellectual achievement. The dinner party will be an interesting cultural exchange between people, showcasing the depth and breadth of human wisdom and creativity across centuries.
